g-polls that same identity and returns progress or its terminal receipt, while foreground host_run is submit-and-attach over the identical durable run.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Text and JSON foreground attachment preserve existing routing contracts: text host stdout streams once to stdout, JSON keeps stdout to one result object while transcript streams to stderr, and provider usage and passthrough errors remain honestly represented.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:happy:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"Use POSIX process groups for TERM/KILL/reap/residual checks, fail before spawn on unsupported platforms, launch Codex with documented explicit stdin -, preserve provider usage parsing and configured timeout ceilings, and separate worker heartbeat from provider progress visibility.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[\"packages/main/src/core/codex-review-leaf.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/host-run.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/managed-host-run.ts\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/managed-host-run-process-smoke.ts\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/provider-codex-smoke.ts\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-003\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"docs/host-run-usage.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/tier-c-crosshost-quorum-execution-plan.md\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Supervise provider processes portably and honestly\",\"userSees\":\"The user sees a silent provider stay running until a real exit or the absolute deadline; cancel/timeout results explicitly report TERM/KILL/reap/residual; Codex execution uses stdin \\\"-\\\" and does not wait on unclosed input.\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Simulate PID or PGID reuse and a mismatched spawn fingerprint at reconcile time; the supervisor must not signal the ambiguous process, must record residual unknown and replacementSafe false, and must not authorize automatic replacement.\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\