ch site refuses pre-spawn until the slot is released.\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"With the ledger enabled, provider admission remains the same while hard-budget decisions, blocked rows, final provider usage, and append failures retain their existing fail-closed and diagnostic-honesty semantics.\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:happy:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"cross_host_review retains snapshot/policy/redacted-env/structured-verdict ownership but delegates execution to ManagedHostRun under the privileged cross-host-verdict profile, attaches to terminal truth, validates verdict shape, and preserves existing timeout policy ceiling and fail-closed semantics.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[\"packages/main/src/core/codex-review-leaf.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/types.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/cross-host-review.ts\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/cross-host-review-smoke.ts\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-005\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"docs/requirements/decisions/review-assurance-floor-execution-plan.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/tier-c-crosshost-quorum-execution-plan.md\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Route cross-host review through managed execution\",\"userSees\":\"cross_host_review still returns the original paired host verdict and jointDecision; its host-B result now also carries a traceable managed-run receipt, and existing policy timeout ceiling and blocked/error wording stay unchanged.\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Try to bypass the privileged profile with a caller-supplied command, cwd, environment, output path, or verdict binding; cross_host_review remains owner of snapshot, policy, redacted environment, and verdict validation, and ManagedHostRun executes only the opaque approved profile.\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Race material drift and cancellation after submission but before verdict persistence; stale or cancelled terminal output cannot be submitted as a current host verdict, and the joint decision remains blocked.\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:adversarial:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Prove cross_host_review no longer owns a second direct Codex spawn or kill stack by a source-contract test that fails if production execution bypasses ManagedHostRun.\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:adversarial:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"Return malformed JSON, schema-invalid verdicts, a mismatched material hash, empty output, and abnormal provider exit; each must synthesize the existing blocked host-B verdict and fail closed while retaining only bounded digest or redacted diagnostics.\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Exercise configured cross_host_review timeout ceilings and bounded attempts at their exact boundaries; migration to ManagedHostRun must preserve the existing ceiling, attempt count, and joint-decision behavior while replacing only execution supervision.\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:edge:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Keep Codex silent but alive inside the policy ceiling; cross_host_review must report the managed run as active rather than converting silence into codex_review_no_parseable_verdict before the configured deadline.\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:edge:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"Run cross_host_review through the privileged managed profile with a fixed material snapshot and valid structured Codex verdict; it must attach to the managed terminal receipt, validate the verdict, submit the host-B result, and preserve an agreeing joint pass without exposing raw provider output.\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"End the cross_host_review caller while its provider is still working, then resume by the managed run identity; the same review completes and is consumed once, with no duplicate Codex launch and no verdict loss caused by the caller boundary.\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:happy:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"Extend dispatch/reviewer evidence contracts with a two-phase managed-review protocol. The provider reviewer writes a profile-bound evidence proposal (pass or findings plus truthful read evidence) into the run evidence journal; it never calls final review_pass_set/finding_add before terminal. After successful terminal seals the journal, a mechanical importer verifies exact story/reviewRun/lane/provider/prompt-envelope/material/terminal bindings and imports the provider-authored proposal without letting the controller change its verdict or impersonate the reviewer. Register the new gate-consumed managed receipt/composite evidence class in the shared Proof Admissibility artifact/intake/evaluator contract as well as process-fact registry. Raw CLI, controller-authored substitutes, and heuristic time-window ledger matches cannot satisfy managed evidence; structured degraded decisions remain explicit.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[\"packages/main/src/core/managed-review-evidence.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/managed-review-evidence.ts\"],\"modify\":[\"packages/main/src/core/evidence/admissibility/index.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/finding-verify.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/process-fact-levels.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/process-fact-registry.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/proof-admissibility-gates.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/proof-admissibility.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/review-run.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/types.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/finding.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/review-run.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/story-dispatch.ts\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/managed-review-evidence-smoke.ts\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/proof-admissibility-registry-smoke.ts\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/review-pass-discard-smoke.ts\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/review-run-smoke.ts\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-006\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"docs/requirements/decisions/proof-admissibility-hardening-execution-plan.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/review-assurance-floor-execution-plan.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/review-run-binding-race.md\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Bind formal reviewer evidence to exact managed receipts\",\"userSees\":\"A CLI reviewer provider-authored pass/finding proposal is imported mechanically after that run reaches a successful terminal and is sealed; an exact receipt match is accepted by the REVIEW gate, while raw CLI, controller-authored, non-terminal, forged, stale, and cross-story/lane/provider evidence is rejected with a concrete remediation.\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Controller non-impersonation E2E: after provider proposal creation, attempt every controller-supplied verdict, note, finding, evidenceState, reviewer identity, readManifest/readLog or provenance override and attempt direct controller final review_pass_set/finding_add as the managed reviewer; the importer exposes no such override surface, rejects altered bytes or identity, preserves the provider-authored proposal exactly, and never records the controller as reviewer.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Tamper each bound field independently, forge runId/terminal/proposal/journal digests, append or truncate journal bytes, swap receipts across story/reviewRun/lane/provider/prompt/material, or replay stale material; every variant is rejected by both import admission and REVIEW consumption while the byte-authentic control is accepted.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:adversarial:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Shared-evaluator mutation contract: delete or bypass the shared Proof Admissibility intake/evaluator call at either import-time or REVIEW-gate consumption, hard-code an allow result, introduce a managed-review-only registry or parallel evaluator, or diverge a canonical reason code; the source/registry contract and mutation smoke must fail for every mutant, proving both boundaries consume one registry/intake/evaluator instead of mirrored special cases.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:adversarial:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Submit raw bash plus provider CLI output, usage-ledger rows, matching provider/time-window metadata, controller-authored proof-looking fields, main/implementer evidence, or an unsealed provider proposal as the managed composite evidence; none may satisfy import, review_pass_set/finding provenance, REVIEW assurance or gate evidence, and each refusal uses a registered canonical remediation reason.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:adversarial:3\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Race proposal publication, terminal creation, journal sealing and import while attempting a late proposal replacement; import cannot begin before the successful exclusive terminal covers the final proposal and journal digests, post-seal writes are rejected or integrity-invalid, and exactly one immutable provider-authored evidence identity can become gate-consumed.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:adversarial:4\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"A missing terminal, pre-terminal proposal, failed/cancelled/timed_out/nonzero terminal, incomplete or ambiguous cleanup, missing proposal, or multiple proposals must receive the matching canonical Proof Admissibility refusal and import no ReviewPass/Finding; diagnostic or degraded evidence remains explicit and cannot upgrade to normal managed assurance.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"After a valid import, change materialHash, storyFilesHash, head lineage, prompt envelope, review round, lane policy, provider binding, proposal bytes or journal bytes; both a fresh import attempt and REVIEW-gate revalidation must fail closed through the shared evaluator with the same canonical stale/integrity/consumer reason family rather than trust a persisted boolean.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:edge:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Replay the same authentic runId/receipt and race two importers; import is idempotent and converges on one exact ReviewPass or finding set with unchanged provider reviewer/read provenance, while a different receipt cannot supersede or rewrite the already imported provider proposal.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:edge:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Native-host reviewer lanes retain their existing signed ReviewRun/pass/finding path, while an explicitly configured degraded-single-host result remains local and non-authority, names the absent managed composite evidence, and is never relabeled as provider-authored managed or two-host assurance.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:edge:3\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"E2E pass path: the dispatched provider reviewer, while the managed run is active, authors exactly one immutable profile-bound proposal containing its pass verdict, registered reviewer identity, truthful readManifest/readLog, and exact story/reviewRun/lane/provider/prompt-envelope/material bindings; it writes no final ReviewPass. A successful terminal exclusively seals the proposal and append-only journal digests before managed_review_evidence_import accepts only the runId/receipt, and the importer creates the existing ReviewPass without changing verdict or authorship while preserving reviewer, lane, reviewRun and read provenance; the REVIEW gate accepts that exact current composite evidence.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"E2E finding path: the provider reviewer authors immutable findings and read provenance in one sealed proposal, successful terminal precedes import, and the mechanical importer reproduces each provider-authored finding exactly with its reviewer/reviewRun/lane/read provenance; verified open high or critical findings remain visible to the normal REVIEW blocking predicates and cannot be replaced by a controller-authored pass.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:happy:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"E2E admissibility path: import-time admission and later REVIEW-gate consumption both resolve the managed receipt/composite evidence through the same shared Proof Admissibility artifact registry, intake normalization, evaluator, producer/scope/claim/consumer/material policies, and canonical reason-code vocabulary; an authentic control receives the same admissible classification at both boundaries.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:happy:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"Test background continuation beyond caller lifetime, silent-but-live runs, worker crash with deadline reconciliation, cancellation races, process-tree cleanup, slot contention with ledger off, candidate overflow, forged/stale receipts and protected timeout preservation. Document operator status/cancel/recovery, legacy_unmanaged classification, trust boundary and rollout compatibility.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[\"docs/requirements/decisions/managed-cross-provider-cli-execution.md\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/managed-host-run-suite-smoke.ts\"],\"modify\":[\"docs/host-run-usage.md\",\"packages/main/src/core/runtime-artifact-registry.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/doctor.ts\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/managed-host-run-suite-smoke.ts\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-007\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"docs/host-run-usage.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/proof-admissibility-hardening-execution-plan.md\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Add adversarial coverage, observability, migration docs and rollout controls\",\"userSees\":\"Docs and doctor clearly explain that 30 seconds is a single wait cap, silence is not failure, how the absolute deadline converges, and when replacementSafe applies; one aggregate smoke shows the managed host-run full path as PASS.\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"The integrated regression matrix includes silent-but-live execution beyond the former ten-minute observation boundary, worker crash, process-tree TERM-resistant cleanup, ledger-off slot contention, candidate overflow, async EPIPE, and no-output cases; each asserts no duplicate restart and finite terminal convergence.\",\"id\":\"CHK-007:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"The receipt negative-control matrix rejects forged, stale, cross-story, cross-lane, altered-journal, raw CLI, and heuristic ledger evidence while accepting the exact authentic managed receipt; removing any binding check must make the suite fail.\",\"id\":\"CHK-007:adversarial:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"CLI watchdog tests prove runtimeContinuation applies only to declared managed continuation commands: caller idle or max boundaries detach observation without killing the provider, while unrelated commands and explicit configured subprocess deadlines retain their existing enforcement.\",\"id\":\"CHK-007:adversarial:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"A worker-crash real-process smoke plus next-touch reconciliation proves eventual failed or timed_out convergence, while a cancellation-race smoke proves one terminal; both expose runId, deadlineAt, terminal reason, residual and replacementSafe to operators.\",\"id\":\"CHK-007:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Runtime retention removes expired prompt and live-output material under documented policy while preserving the bounded terminal receipt and evidence references needed for audit; doctor classifies missing or corrupt runtime artifacts without treating them as success.\",\"id\":\"CHK-007:edge:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Migration inventory labels every remaining provider execution surface managed or legacy_unmanaged, preserves protected provider and cross_host_review timeout ceilings, and documents unsupported platforms plus the same-uid local trust ceiling without claiming cryptographic or authority proof.\",\"id\":\"CHK-007:edge:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"An end-to-end real-process smoke submits a run, ends the caller boundary, observes the same run from a new caller with no duplicate spawn, and reaches explicit completed terminal truth whose exact receipt is accepted by the intended formal reviewer consumer.\",\"id\":\"CHK-007:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Operator documentation and diagnostics show how to submit detached work, inspect bounded status, distinguish worker heartbeat from provider progress, cancel, interpret deadline and residual states, decide whether replacement is safe, and recover without restarting on silence.\",\"id\":\"CHK-007:happy:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}}],\"description\":\"Implement the approved ManagedHostRun boundary for CLI-launched cross-provider agents: durable detached/foreground execution, bounded status and cancellation, absolute deadlines, process-group cleanup, honest orphan/replacement safety, ledger-independent shared admission, and exact managed-run receipt binding for formal reviewer evidence. This supersedes heuristic time-window provenance matching such as the inactive B-1be5 proposal; it does not manage native host subagents and must preserve legacy configured provider timeout ceilings.\",\"headHash\":\"935bb94e021cb57ceb1534296a3f0d171c59ea1c\",\"materialHash\":\"7719e483312ba65ad131681ebc66189225d3fdfd136f63f775347f458485abee\",\"phase\":\"REVIEW\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"schemaVersion\":\"proofbound.full-task-context.v1\",\"scope\":{\"allowedCreate\":[\"docs/requirements/decisions/managed-cross-provider-cli-execution.md\",\"packages/main/src/core/managed-host-run.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/managed-review-evidence.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/provider-process-admission.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/provider-process-registry.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/managed-review-evidence.ts\"],\"allowedModify\":[\"docs/host-run-usage.md\",\"packages/main/src/cli-engine.ts\",\"packages/main/src/cli/command-catalog.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/agent-dispatch-registry.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/autopilot-executor.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/codex-review-leaf.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/command-policy.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/config.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/evidence/admissibility/index.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/finding-verify.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/host-execution-readiness.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/host-run.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/lattice-brand.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/lattice-dispatch.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/planned-steps-executor.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/process-fact-levels.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/process-fact-registry.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/prompt-role-contract-registry.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/proof-admissibility-gates.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/proof-admissibility.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/review-run.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/runtime-artifact-registry.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/types.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/candidate-spec-routing.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/cross-host-review.ts

