./.lattice/story/actives/B-70e9/review-passes.json:508:      "note": "F-011 fix re-review (round 6, commit e27341a4ff), scope=core/host-run.ts+handlers/host-run.ts+tasks/host-run-usage-smoke.ts+docs/host-run-usage.md. Verified: (1) cwd refusal (host-run.ts:894-896) fires before resolvePhase/assertReviewRunIdBinding (pure, no I/O) and before the first ledger write recordDispatchPreflight (line 1001) -- honest pre-spawn throw, not a recorded blocked row, matching the header contract; smoke asserts no ledger dir exists after refusal. (2) cwd propagation is single-source: handler binds cwd:ctx.root literally alongside root:ctx.root (same variable, cannot diverge); core threads args.cwd into the one HostRunSpawnPlan built inside invokeRunner (both ledger ON/OFF paths); defaultHostRunRunner passes plan.cwd directly into child_process.spawn; no other production caller of runHostRun/defaultHostRunRunner exists; no process.cwd() calls remain in either runtime file. (3) resolveStoryCommandWorkspace non-use is justified: confirmed in handlers/context.ts it requires storyId (throws for adhoc host_run) and itself calls process.cwd() internally -- exactly what this fix eliminates. (4) new smoke realpath handling is correct on both sides (process.cwd() is already OS-canonicalized after chdir, verified empirically; both comparisons realpath the plan/child side) so macOS /tmp-symlink cannot produce a false pass/fail. (5) no dead code: realpathSync import used, tsc build clean, no as any in any of the 4 changed files. Reran build (clean), test:host-run-usage (36/36 incl. both new F-011 checks), test:usage-sweep (16/16, unaffected). No blockers.",
