./.lattice/story/actives/B-137a/findings.json:302:      "desc": "doc-promise-undelivered: packages/main/src/core/provider-process-registry.ts:298 and packages/main/src/tasks/provider-process-registry-smoke.ts:22-31 still restrict the provider-surface classifier and productionSources traversal to core/handlers/providers, although the production tree also contains cli/, verifier/, and top-level entrypoints. Therefore the stated contract that any new direct provider spawn in production fails the inventory smoke is false: the exported classifier returns core=true but cli=false, verifier=false, top=false for identical node:child_process + spawn(\"codex\", [\"exec\"]) source, while provider-process-registry-smoke still passes. This is the unresolved F-002 class and leaves future direct CLI/verifier provider launches mechanically invisible; enumerate every production .ts source (excluding tests/generated output) and classify false positives explicitly, and add non-core regression mutants.",
