./.lattice/story/actives/B-70e9/review-passes.json:1579:      "note": "Round 18 re-review of F-025/F-026 fix (387b0ad3a2). Scrutinized: token verify windows in acquireHostRunSlot/scanLiveSlots/releaseSlot (re-verify-then-unlink always immediately precedes the syscall, sameSlotOccupant correctly compares pid+token for valid occupants and state-only for missing/corrupt); scanLiveSlots reporting semantics after the narrowing (never surfaces token, correctly reports legacy token-less live slots, reclaim-then-report loop correctly skips reclaimed entries); legacy token-less slot handling (readSlotOccupant returns token:null for pre-fix meta, exercised by the seedSlot smoke helper and the live-holder-protection test, reclaim/report logic is token-independent so no special-casing needed and none is missing); all three caller sites (host-run.ts:1238, autopilot-executor.ts:414, codex-review-leaf.ts:649) thread {file,token} consistently via the new AcquiredHostRunSlot type, no leftover single-arg releaseSlot calls anywhere in src; UsageLineScanner truncatedSinceLastCandidate set/clear sites (set on every over-cap drop at both the no-newline and newline branches, cleared only when consider() actually retains a usage-bearing candidate, ordinary non-usage lines and drop-only leave it untouched) matching the documented F-013/F-026 last-usage-wins semantics; docs/host-run-usage.md prose for both fixes matches code exactly (pid-liveness-only reclaim for valid meta, mtime backstop scoped to missing/corrupt meta, token-guarded release, candidate-relative truncation). No dead code, no as-any, no empty catches (all catches carry an explaining comment consistent with the best-effort doctrine) in the touched files. npm run build clean. test:host-run-usage 61/61, test:usage-sweep 17/17, cross-host-review-smoke 24/24, autopilot-v2-reliability-smoke PASS. Zero open findings across all 25 story findings (all resolved with strong evidence). No blocking issues found.",
./.lattice/story/actives/B-70e9/findings.json:166:      "desc": "core/host-run.ts:770-777 defaultHostRunRunner: onChunk (and therefore the handler's passthrough, which does raw process.stdout.write/process.stderr.write) is invoked synchronously inside the child.stdout/stderr 'data' listeners with no try/catch. If the passthrough sink throws (e.g. EPIPE when a downstream consumer of host_run output closes early, a common real-world case for `lattice host_run | head` or a killed reviewer pipe), the exception is uncaught inside a Node EventEmitter callback and crashes the whole process: the spawned child is orphaned (no SIGKILL, since finish() in the same runner never runs), runHostRun's `finally { releaseSlot(slotFile) }` (host-run.ts:1008-1010) never executes so the concurrency slot leaks until the staleness backstop reclaims it hours later, and no ledger final row is written. No global uncaughtException/EPIPE handler exists anywhere in packages/main/src to catch this. Fix direction: wrap the onChunk call (or the passthrough sink itself, in both defaultHostRunRunner and the handler's passthrough) in try/catch so a downstream write failure degrades gracefully instead of crashing the host run and leaking the slot.",
./.lattice/story/actives/B-70e9/findings.json:361:      "resolvedReason": "Commit 3f3dea9bcd: runClaudeRepair ledger-ON path now runs the same admission chain as runHostRun in the same order (preflight -> recordBudgetBlock -> acquireHostRunSlot -> spawn -> releaseSlot in finally), returning an honest failed attempt (exitCode 3, reason in stderrExcerpt) without spawning on refusal; slot-registry errors fail closed without faking cap rows. Ledger OFF byte-identical (env-pinned in smoke). host-run smoke 44/44 with failing-before proven by reverting the file; budget-smoke import fence gained autopilot-executor as the third authorized recordBudgetBlock site.",
./.lattice/story/actives/B-70e9/findings.json:384:      "resolvedReason": "Commit b5df58d44d: codex-review-leaf ledger-ON path now runs the same admission chain as host_run/autopilot-repair (preflight -> recordBudgetBlock provider openai -> acquireHostRunSlot -> spawn -> releaseSlot in finally); refusal synthesizes a decision=blocked verdict (reason budget_blocked/concurrency_cap_exceeded, exitCode 3, no spawn, no fabricated pass/fail) which cross_host_review surfaces as hostB=blocked / joint=blocked; slot-registry errors fail closed without fake cap rows; budget-smoke fence gained the leaf as the fourth authorized recordBudgetBlock site. Failing-before proven with admission neutralized (all 3 new checks fail); host-run smoke 47/47, cross-host-review 24, budget 41, dispatch 40.",
./.lattice/story/actives/B-70e9/findings.json:544:      "desc": "[codex host-B, cross_host_review B-70e9-xhr-r15] Stale live slot release can delete a newer holder admission slot: the slot registry reclaims a slot when its mtime exceeds staleMs even if the recorded pid is ALIVE, reusing the same fixed slot-N path; the original long-running holder later calls releaseSlot(file) which blindly unlinks whatever is at that path - deleting a different live run slot and letting subsequent runs bypass the concurrency cap. Same ownership class as F-018 but on the slot registry. Fix direction: ownership token in SlotMeta verified by releaseSlot before unlink (mirror the ledger lock release guard), and stop reclaiming live-pid slots by age alone; regression where a live stale slot is reclaimed/reacquired and the original holder late release must not remove the new holder slot.",
./.lattice/story/actives/B-70e9/findings.json:559:      "resolvedReason": "Commit 387b0ad3a2: slot registry mirrors the F-018 ownership design - acquireHostRunSlot mints a UUID token into the slot record and returns {file, token}; releaseSlot(file, token) read-verifies before unlink (mismatch/missing backs off); staleness narrowed to pid-liveness-only for valid-meta slots (LIVE never age-reclaimed, dead reclaimed at any age; mtime backstop only for missing/corrupt meta) in BOTH acquire and scanLiveSlots; reclaim re-verifies the occupant immediately before unlink. All three callers (host_run, autopilot repair, codex review leaf) thread the handle. Failing-before proven on pre-fix dist: live 7h slot stolen; late release deleted the new holder slot and cap admitted a third run. host-run smoke 61 checks.",
